  "Faux quand a < 0 : arg(−1 + i) = 3π/4, mais arctan(−1) = −π/4. Il faut corriger de π.": "False when a < 0: arg(−1 + i) = 3π/4, but arctan(−1) = −π/4. You must correct by π.",
  "Pour tous réels θ et φ : e^(iθ)·e^(iφ) = e^(i(θ + φ)).": "For all reals θ and φ: e^(iθ)·e^(iφ) = e^(i(θ + φ)).",
  "C'est la règle d'addition : cos(θ + φ) + i sin(θ + φ).": "It is the addition rule: cos(θ + φ) + i sin(θ + φ).",
  "Pour tout réel θ : |e^(iθ)| = 1.": "For every real θ: |e^(iθ)| = 1.",
  "Pour tout z ≠ 0 : z = |z|·e^(i·arg z).": "For every z ≠ 0: z = |z|·e^(i·arg z).",
  "C'est la forme exponentielle : r = |z| et θ = arg z.": "It is the exponential form: r = |z| and θ = arg z.",
  "Pour tout réel θ : e^(iθ) + e^(−iθ) = 2cos θ.": "For every real θ: e^(iθ) + e^(−iθ) = 2cos θ.",
  "Les parties imaginaires i sin θ et −i sin θ s'annulent.": "The imaginary parts i sin θ and −i sin θ cancel.",
  "Pour tous z, w ≠ 0 : arg(z·w) = arg z + arg w (arguments dans ]−π ; π]).": "For all z, w ≠ 0: arg(z·w) = arg z + arg w (arguments in ]−π ; π]).",
  "Avec z = w = −1 : arg(1) = 0, mais π + π = 2π. L'égalité n'est vraie qu'à 2π près.": "With z = w = −1: arg(1) = 0, but π + π = 2π. The equality only holds up to 2π.",
  "Pour tout z ≠ 0 : arg(−z) = arg z + π (arguments dans ]−π ; π]).": "For every z ≠ 0: arg(−z) = arg z + π (arguments in ]−π ; π]).",
